@startuml
title Route-Based Beacon Navigation - Data Structure UML

class StateMachine_t {
    +State_t* state
    +bool isBusy
    +State_t* buffer[QUEUE_CAPACITY]
    +fifo_t queue
}

class State_t {
    +entry(StateMachine_t* sm)
    +main(StateMachine_t* sm)
    +exit(StateMachine_t* sm)
    +char* name
}

class RouteProfile_t {
    +RouteId_t id
    +char* displayName
    +RouteBeaconRule_t* rules
    +uint8_t ruleCount
    +State_t* nextState
}

class RouteBeaconRule_t {
    +BeaconId_t beaconId
    +BeaconRole_t role
    +int rssiThreshold
}

class BeaconDefinition_t {
    +BeaconId_t id
    +char* mac
    +char* label
}

class BeaconScan_t {
    +BeaconId_t id
    +int rssi
    +bool valid
}

class BeaconNavigator_t {
    +RouteProfile_t* activeRoute
    +int bestRssi
    +int currentAvgRssi
    +bool targetSeen
    +bool targetNear
    +navigation_set_route()
    +navigation_update()
    +navigation_get_next_state()
}

class InputBuffer_t {
    +char buffer[16]
    +uint8_t index
    +bool submitted
}

enum BeaconRole_t {
    IGNORE
    PASS_BY
    APPROACH
    TARGET
    WRONG_WAY
}

enum BeaconId_t {
    B01
    B02
    B03
    B04
    B05
    B06
    B07
    B08
    B09
    B10
}

enum RouteId_t {
    START_TO_EXPERIENCE
    EXPERIENCE_TO_MATERIAL_QUESTION
    MATERIAL_QUESTION_TO_COLLECTION
    COLLECTION_TO_BUILD_TEST
    BUILD_TEST_TO_FINISH
}

StateMachine_t --> State_t : current state
StateMachine_t --> State_t : queued states
State_t --> StateMachine_t : receives sm pointer

RouteProfile_t --> RouteBeaconRule_t : contains rules
RouteBeaconRule_t --> BeaconRole_t : has role
RouteBeaconRule_t --> BeaconId_t : references beacon id
RouteProfile_t --> RouteId_t : has route id
RouteProfile_t --> State_t : next mission state

BeaconDefinition_t --> BeaconId_t : physical beacon id
BeaconNavigator_t --> RouteProfile_t : active route
BeaconNavigator_t --> BeaconScan_t : processes scan results

note right of RouteBeaconRule_t
A beacon has no fixed room meaning.

Its meaning is decided by the active route.

Example:
B07 in route A = PASS_BY
B07 in route B = TARGET
end note

note bottom of BeaconNavigator_t
BeaconNavigator stores navigation progress:

bestRssi:
    strongest target RSSI seen so far

currentAvgRssi:
    averaged RSSI from recent scans

targetSeen:
    true after the target beacon is first detected
end note

@enduml